## Using specific codenames (for example: "trixie") rather than generic code
## names (for example: "stable") because grml-debootstrap did not support
## generic code names for --release. See also:
## github.com/grml/grml-debootstrap/issues/37

## Using contrib, because it contains virtualbox-guest-x11.

## Using http://snapshot.debian.org/ to create verifiable builds.
##
## 1. Go to for example:
##    - http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/
##    - http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/
## 2. Then for example click on 2013 09
##    - http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/?year=2013&month=10
##    - http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/?year=2013&month=10
## 3. Scroll down and for example click on 2013-09-19 21:48:59
##    - http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/20130919T215514Z/
##    - http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20130919T214859Z/
## 4. See note above!
##    - See note above!
##    - See note above!

## THE REPRODUCIBILITY PIN. The snapshot.debian.org timestamp below is what makes a
## '--freshness frozen' build reproducible: a third party who builds from this exact commit
## gets the same package versions. approx (127.0.0.1:9977 -> debian-frozen) is a generic,
## UNPINNED pass-through to snapshot.debian.org; the timestamp is a path segment HERE, so this
## file is the single reviewable place the pin changes. Bump it (to a newer valid snapshot)
## with dm-maintenance, not by hand and not in approx.conf.
## trixie-updates is included (pinned to the same snapshot) so the frozen build
## matches the trixie-updates the build machine already carries: without it,
## build_machine_setup could only offer an older stdlib (e.g. python3.13
## deb13u2) than the docker base image pulled from trixie-updates (deb13u4),
## producing "held broken packages". trixie-updates lives in the main archive
## (debian-frozen), same URI as trixie.
Types: deb
URIs: http://127.0.0.1:9977/debian-frozen/20260720T082444Z
Suites: trixie trixie-updates
Components: main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
Enabled: yes
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg

Types: deb
URIs: http://127.0.0.1:9977/debian-security-frozen/20260720T082444Z
Suites: trixie-security
Components: main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
Enabled: yes
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg

## We currently do not need any source packages for builds.
